---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
const addr = site.address;
---
<Base title="Terms and conditions" description="The terms for using Little Brains games and the littlebrains.co website.">
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">The small print</p>
      <h1>Terms and conditions</h1>
      <p class="lede">Last updated {site.legalUpdated}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-bottom: 96px">
    <div class="narrow prose">
      <div class="summary-box">
        <p><strong>The short version</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Our games are licensed to you through the App Store under Apple's standard licence. These terms add a few things about how we work.</li>
          <li>Apple takes all payments and handles refunds. Each game's App Store page says whether its extras are a one-time purchase or a subscription.</li>
          <li>What you've already bought stays yours. New features added later may need a separate purchase or a subscription.</li>
          <li>Your legal rights as a consumer aren't affected by anything here.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <nav class="toc" aria-label="Contents">
        <strong>Contents</strong>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#about">About these terms</a></li>
          <li><a href="#licence">Your licence to our games</a></li>
          <li><a href="#purchases">Prices and purchases</a></li>
          <li><a href="#codes">Gifts and codes</a></li>
          <li><a href="#rights">Your consumer rights</a></li>
          <li><a href="#children">Children and grown-ups</a></li>
          <li><a href="#fair-use">Fair use</a></li>
          <li><a href="#ours">What's ours</a></li>
          <li><a href="#website">This website</a></li>
          <li><a href="#liability">Our responsibility to you</a></li>
          <li><a href="#availability">Devices, availability and withdrawing a game</a></li>
          <li><a href="#changes">Updates and changes</a></li>
          <li><a href="#control">Events outside our control</a></li>
          <li><a href="#ideas">Your ideas and feedback</a></li>
          <li><a href="#other">Other important terms</a></li>
          <li><a href="#law">Law and disputes</a></li>
          <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <h2 id="about">1. About these terms</h2>
      <p>These terms cover the Little Brains games for iPhone and iPad ("our games") and this website, littlebrains.co. Little Brains is run by {site.owner}, in {site.country} ("we", "us"). Contact: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>{addr && <>. Address: {addr}</>}.</p>
      <p>By downloading one of our games or using this website, you agree to these terms. Please read them with our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="licence">2. Your licence to our games</h2>
      <p>Our games are licensed, not sold. Your licence to use each game is granted under Apple's <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/">Licensed Application End User License Agreement</a> (the "Standard EULA"), which you accept when you download from the App Store. These terms add to the Standard EULA; if the two ever conflict about your licence to use a game, the Standard EULA wins.</p>
      <p>The licence is between you and us, not Apple. We, not Apple, are responsible for our games, their content, and any support and maintenance.</p>

      <h2 id="purchases">3. Prices and purchases</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Free to try.</strong> Our games are free to download and include some free content, unless a game's App Store page says otherwise.</li>
        <li><strong>Unlocks and subscriptions.</strong> More content can be unlocked with an in-app purchase. Depending on the game, that's a one-time purchase or a subscription; the App Store shows which, and the price in your currency including any taxes, before you confirm.</li>
        <li><strong>What you've bought stays yours.</strong> A one-time purchase keeps everything it included when you bought it, in every later version of the game, at no extra cost. We won't move it behind a subscription or ask you to pay for it again.</li>
        <li><strong>New features may cost extra.</strong> Updates may add new content or features. Some may be free, and some may need an additional one-time purchase or a subscription. Anything that costs extra will be clearly marked, and buying it is always your choice.</li>
        <li><strong>Subscriptions</strong>, where a game offers one, renew automatically at the end of each period until you cancel. You can cancel at any time in your Apple Account settings, at least 24 hours before the renewal date, and you keep access until the end of the period you've paid for.</li>
        <li><strong>Apple takes payment.</strong> All purchases are made through the App Store and are subject to Apple's <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/">Media Services Terms and Conditions</a>. We never see your payment details.</li>
        <li><strong>Restoring.</strong> An unlock belongs to the Apple Account that bought it and can be restored on your other devices signed in to that account, from the grown-ups' area of the game.</li>
        <li><strong>Family Sharing.</strong> Where a game says so on the App Store, an unlock can be shared with your Family Sharing group.</li>
        <li><strong>Refunds.</strong> Apple handles refunds. Request one at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="codes">4. Gifts and codes</h2>
      <p>From time to time we may give out codes that unlock content in our games, for example as gifts or prizes. Codes are redeemed through the App Store, work once, can't be exchanged for money and may have an expiry date, which we'll tell you when we give you the code.</p>
      <p>We don't sell codes on this website or through anyone else. If someone offers to sell you a Little Brains code, it may not work, and we can't help with it. To give one of our games as a present, an Apple Gift Card is the simplest way to cover the unlock.</p>

      <h2 id="rights">5. Your consumer rights</h2>
      <p>If you're a consumer in the UK, the Consumer Rights Act 2015 gives you rights in digital content: it must be of satisfactory quality, fit for purpose and as described. If a game isn't, tell us and we'll try to fix it; you may also be entitled to a refund, which Apple will process. Nothing in these terms affects your legal rights.</p>

      <h2 id="children">6. Children and grown-ups</h2>
      <p>Our games are made for children to play, with a grown-up's say-so. A parent or guardian is responsible for downloading our games, for any purchases, and for the settings in the grown-ups' area. Purchases and settings sit behind a grown-ups' gate, and you can also use Apple's Screen Time and Ask to Buy to control purchases.</p>

      <h2 id="fair-use">7. Fair use</h2>
      <p>Please don't copy, sell, share or redistribute our games or their pictures, try to get around purchases, or reverse-engineer or modify our games, except where the law allows you to.</p>

      <h2 id="ours">8. What's ours</h2>
      <p>Our games, their pictures, sounds and code, the Little Brains name and this website belong to us or to people who have licensed them to us. Fonts on this website are used under the SIL Open Font License.</p>

      <h2 id="website">9. This website</h2>
      <p>You're welcome to browse and link to this website. We try to keep it accurate and available, but we may change or remove pages at any time. Links to other websites, such as the App Store, are there for convenience; we aren't responsible for their content.</p>

      <h2 id="liability">10. Our responsibility to you</h2>
      <p>We're responsible for loss or damage you suffer that is a foreseeable result of us breaking these terms or failing to use reasonable care and skill. We're not responsible for loss or damage that wasn't foreseeable.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>For home use only.</strong> Our games are for domestic and private use. We're not responsible for any business losses, such as lost profit, income or opportunity.</li>
        <li><strong>Progress saved on your device.</strong> Games save progress on your device only. We're not responsible for progress lost when a game is deleted, or a device is reset, lost, replaced or restored from a backup that doesn't include it.</li>
        <li><strong>A limit on what we pay.</strong> Apart from the cases in the next paragraph, our total responsibility to you for anything to do with a game is limited to the amount you paid for that game and its purchases.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We don't exclude or limit our liability where it would be unlawful to do so, including for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, for fraud, or for your legal rights as a consumer, including those described in section 5.</p>

      <h2 id="availability">11. Devices, availability and withdrawing a game</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Supported devices.</strong> Each game's App Store page lists the devices and the iOS or iPadOS versions it needs. We aim to keep our games working with new versions, but we can't promise they'll work on every future version or on older devices.</li>
        <li><strong>Withdrawing a game.</strong> We may stop selling a game, stop updating it or remove it from the App Store, for example if it can no longer be supported. If we do, a game you've already downloaded keeps working on your device for as long as your device supports it, together with everything you bought in it, and you can usually download it again from your purchase history in the App Store.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="changes">12. Updates and changes</h2>
      <p>We may update our games to fix problems, improve them or keep them working with new versions of iOS and iPadOS. Some updates may be needed for a game to keep working. We may also change what our games include, for example by adding advertising or analytics. If we do, we'll update our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> and the App Store listing before that version is released. We may also update these terms; the date at the top shows when they last changed. If a change materially affects you, we'll explain it here before it applies.</p>

      <h2 id="control">13. Events outside our control</h2>
      <p>We're not responsible for delays or problems caused by events outside our reasonable control, such as a failure of Apple's App Store or payment systems, an internet or power outage, or a change Apple makes to iOS or iPadOS. If that happens, we'll tell you where we can and do what we reasonably can to limit the effect.</p>

      <h2 id="ideas">14. Your ideas and feedback</h2>
      <p>We love hearing ideas for new games, pictures and features. If you send us an idea or feedback, you agree that we may use it, change it and build on it, without paying you or crediting you. Please don't send us anything you want to keep confidential or that belongs to someone else.</p>

      <h2 id="other">15. Other important terms</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Transferring these terms.</strong> We may transfer our rights and responsibilities under these terms to another organisation, for example if we form a company to run Little Brains. We'll make sure it doesn't reduce your rights. You can't transfer your rights under these terms to someone else, except through Family Sharing where a game offers it.</li>
        <li><strong>Nobody else has rights under these terms.</strong> These terms are between you and us. No one else has any right to enforce them.</li>
        <li><strong>If a court finds part of these terms invalid,</strong> the rest of them stay in force.</li>
        <li><strong>If we don't enforce these terms straight away,</strong> we can still enforce them later.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="law">16. Law and disputes</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the law of {site.governingLaw}. If you live in Scotland or Northern Ireland, you can bring proceedings in your local courts. If you live elsewhere, you keep any protections your local law gives you. If something goes wrong, please contact us first; we'd much rather sort it out together.</p>

      <h2 id="contact">17. Contact</h2>
      <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. We aim to reply within {site.replyTime}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
